From 815da079eaa7861fd0616e129f2137296977cd6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@localhost>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:20:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bluetooth: mark local extended features page 2 broken on
 Biscuit

The MT8163 controller advertises max_page 2 in its Read Local Extended
Features page 1 reply, then answers the page 2 read with status 0x30,
Parameter Out Of Mandatory Range. bt_to_errno() has no mapping for 0x30,
so it falls through to ENOSYS; hci_read_local_ext_features_all_sync()
treats that as fatal and hci_dev_open() aborts, leaving hci0 registered
but permanently DOWN with "Opcode 0x1004 failed: -38".

Measured on Device #1 with btmon: the rest of the roughly fifty command
init sequence completes, including Reset, Read Local Supported Features,
extended features page 1, the buffer size and LE reads, and Set Event
Mask. Only the page 2 read fails.

Set HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LOCAL_EXT_FEATURES_PAGE_2 so
hci_cc_read_local_ext_features() leaves hdev->max_page at 1 and the page
2 read is never issued.

No firmware, patch address, fragmentation, STP, BTIF, CONSYS power or
boot packaging behaviour changed.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
index 80147fe..eb71779 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
@@ -1143,6 +1143,14 @@ static int mt8163_stp_hci_register(struct mt8163_stp *stp)
 	SET_HCIDEV_DEV(hdev, stp->dev);
 	hci_set_drvdata(hdev, stp);
 
+	/*
+	 * The controller advertises extended-features max_page 2 but answers a
+	 * page 2 read with 0x30, Parameter Out Of Mandatory Range. That status
+	 * has no bt_to_errno() mapping, so it surfaces as -ENOSYS and aborts
+	 * hci_dev_open(). Cap max_page at 1 so the page 2 read is never issued.
+	 */
+	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LOCAL_EXT_FEATURES_PAGE_2);
+
 	ret = hci_register_dev(hdev);
 	if (ret) {
 		hci_free_dev(hdev);
-- 
